values.content:
=Write one horror monologue of {{ $json.decisions.ask_words }} words, in the style of the EXAMPLE below.

RULES THE EXAMPLE DEMONSTRATES - match every one:
- Sentence one states a specific, concrete, disturbing fact. No weather, no mood, no "I felt".
- One narrator, {{ $json.decisions.tense }} tense, one continuous scene or one confession.
- Short declarative sentences. Concrete nouns. The narrator handles real objects and describes them plainly. No metaphor, no simile.
- Violence is implied, never described. No injury detail, no gore.
- End exactly the way HOW IT ENDS says. Final sentences are action or fact only. No moral, no "I realised", no explaining.

=================== EXAMPLE ===================
BRIEF:
{{ $json.decisions.example_brief }}

MONOLOGUE:
{{ $json.decisions.example_text }}
================= END EXAMPLE =================

NOW WRITE YOUR OWN. Same craft, completely different story:
SUBGENRE: {{ $json.decisions.genre.replace(/_/g, " ") }} - {{ $json.decisions.pitch }}
WHAT MAY APPEAR: {{ $json.decisions.allow }}
THE THREAT: {{ $json.decisions.core }}
SETTING: {{ $json.decisions.setting }}
TENSE: {{ $json.decisions.tense }}
HOW IT ENDS: {{ $json.decisions.ending }}

Output only the monologue. One paragraph, no title.

parameters.jsCode:
// Clean the model output and re-emit it in the shape the parent workflow reads
// ($json.output[0].content[0].text), so ContentGeneration3.0 needs no change.

let text = $json.output?.[0]?.content?.[0]?.text;
if (!text) throw new Error("No model output at output[0].content[0].text");

text = text.trim();

// Mistral-Nemo based models under a ChatML template leak the EOS as text and keep
// going ("</s> [TOOL_CALLS] ..."). Cut at the first trailer token so nothing after
// it can reach the story file or edge-tts.
const TRAILER = /<\/?s>|<\|im_end\|>|<\|eot_id\|>|\[\/?TOOL_CALLS\]|\[\/?INST\]/g;
text = text.split(TRAILER)[0].replace(TRAILER, "").trim();

// Strip markdown fences and any wrapping quotes
text = text.replace(/^```[a-z]*\s*/i, "").replace(/\s*```$/, "").trim();
if (/^["'\u201c].*["'\u201d]$/s.test(text)) text = text.slice(1, -1).trim();

// Strip a leading preamble line ("Here is your story:", "Certainly!", a title)
const lines = text.split("\n");
if (lines.length > 1 && /^(here|sure|certainly|okay|of course|title)\b/i.test(lines[0].trim())) {
  lines.shift();
  text = lines.join("\n").trim();
}

// Normalise typography. Smart quotes and dashes reach edge-tts and the ASS
// subtitle file; ASCII is safer in both.
text = text
  .replace(/[\u2018\u2019\u201b]/g, "'")
  .replace(/[\u201c\u201d]/g, '"')
  .replace(/[\u2013\u2014]/g, " - ")
  .replace(/\u2026/g, "...")
  .replace(/[ \t]+/g, " ")
  .replace(/\n{2,}/g, "\n\n")
  .trim();

const words = text.split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean).length;

// Surfaced for debugging, not enforced. A hard retry loop is not worth the extra
// generation time when 120-200 words is 32-54 seconds either way.
const flagged = ["chill", "spine", "dread", "eerie", "unsettling", "realized", "realised",
   "as if", "seemed", "somehow", "shiver", "blood ran cold", "little did i know", "i felt"]
  .filter(w => new RegExp("\\b" + w, "i").test(text));

return [{ json: {
  output: [{ content: [{ text }] }],   // parent-compatible shape
  wordCount: words,
  estimatedSeconds: +(words / 3.72).toFixed(1),
  flaggedWords: flagged,
  brief: $('Randomizer').item.json.decisions
} }];
